# CreateObject and DeleteObject (§15.3, §15.4).

# An analog-value of the device's choosing, named "Fan"; then one at 7.
00 05 01 0a 0e 09 02 0f 1e 09 4d 2e 75 04 00 46 61 6e 2f 1f => create-object type analog-value with object-name = string "Fan"
00 05 02 0a 0e 1c 00 80 00 07 0f => create-object analog-value:7
30 02 0a c4 00 80 00 07 => create-object-ack analog-value:7
00 05 03 0b c4 00 80 00 07 => delete-object analog-value:7
# Refused at the first initial value: unsupported-object-type (36); and a
# delete refused: object-deletion-not-permitted (23).
50 01 0a 0e 91 01 91 24 0f 19 01 => create-object-error object: unsupported-object-type at 1
50 03 0b 91 01 91 17 => error delete-object: object: object-deletion-not-permitted
# A specifier with neither a type nor an identifier.
00 05 04 0a 0e 0f => error missing-field 1
